cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SteerLab in your research, please cite it as below."
title: SteerLab
abstract: >-
  A concept-steering workbench for open-weight language models: extract named
  concept directions from a model's residual stream, inject them during
  generation at a measured strength, and measure how the outputs move. Two
  independent engines — Swift/MLX on Apple silicon and Python/PyTorch on CUDA
  — share one artifact model, with a hash-pinned, one-way freeze lifecycle so
  that experimental settings are fixed before behavior is measured.
type: software
authors:
  # Named authors can be added here as `- family-names: … / given-names: …`.
  - name: "The SteerLab Authors"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - activation steering
  - interpretability
  - representation engineering
  - large language models
  - reproducibility
